    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0770" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/9–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-16T17:00:00-04:00">September 16,
                            1946—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>755. Reurtel 1448, Sep 10,<anchor n="64" xml:id="d437-f1"/> breakdown post V–J
                    Day military lend-lease aid to China given below. Period covered Sep 2, 1945
                    through Jul 31, 1946. Note that time lag in reporting makes figures
                    incomplete.</p>
                <table cols="2" rend="width: 75%" rendition="#center" rows="8">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Category</hi>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">$ million of aid</hi>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Ordnance &amp; ordnance stores</cell>
                        <cell role="num">64. 1</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Aircraft &amp; Aeronautical material</cell>
                        <cell role="num">11. 3</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Tanks &amp; other vehicles</cell>
                        <cell role="num">88. 6</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Miscellaneous military equipment</cell>
                        <cell role="num">41. 9</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Agricultural, industrial &amp; other commod.</cell>
                        <cell role="num">21. 0</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Services &amp; expenses</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">398. 3</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#float-right">Total</cell>
                        <cell role="num">625. 2</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d437-f1" n="64" xml:id="d437-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested on behalf of T. V. Soong, President of the Chinese
                    Executive Yuan, a breakdown of post V–J Day military lend-lease.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
